al logarithms, determine the value of $x$ that satisfies the equation ${5}^{x-2}={7}^{3-2x}.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534579 true] [17592186296723 1113 #uuid "1bb6b417-40c6-590c-a34f-11b86676b4c8" 13194139534579 true] [17592186296723 1145 "First, we take the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{x-2} & ={7}^{3-2x} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({5}^{x-2}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({7}^{3-2x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the power law of logarithms to simplify both sides of the equation. This gives\n\n$$\n(x-2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)=(3-2x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7).\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5) & =(3-2x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7) \\\\ x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5) & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)-2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7) \\\\ x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)+2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7) & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5) \\\\ x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)) & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7) \\\\ x & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534579 true] [17592186296724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296725 13194139534579 true] [17592186296724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296726 13194139534579 true] [17592186296724 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534579 true] [17592186296724 1041 "field-1" 13194139534579 true] [17592186296724 1104 #edb/ref 17592186296725 13194139534579 true] [17592186296724 1110 #uuid "b4542e3b-9561-594b-b6a3-ccc39c211265" 13194139534579 true] [17592186296725 1034 "\\frac{2\\ln(5)+3\\ln(7)}{\\ln(5)+2\\ln(7)}" 13194139534579 true] [17592186296725 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534579 true] [17592186296725 1111 #uuid "457e08fc-0e12-51ae-bf10-2005db223d04" 13194139534579 true] [17592186296726 1034 "0" 13194139534579 true] [17592186296726 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534579 true] [17592186296726 1111 #uuid "f85bce8d-8241-50a8-8dc7-3a156995ef7b" 13194139534579 true] [17592186296727 1017 #edb/ref 17592186296728 13194139534579 true] [17592186296727 1089 "q-242902" 13194139534579 true] [17592186296727 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534579 true] [17592186296727 1100 "Expressed in terms of natural logarithms, determine the value of $x$ that satisfies the equation ${e}^{x+2}={2}^{x+3}.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534579 true] [17592186296727 1113 #uuid "7c0698ed-83ff-5702-9102-b20873016600" 13194139534579 true] [17592186296727 1145 "First, we take the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x+2} & ={2}^{x+3} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{x+2}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{x+3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{a})=a$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\nx+2=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{x+3}).\n$$\n\nNext, we use the power law of logarithms to simplify the right-hand side:\n\n$$\nx+2=(x+3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2 & =(x+3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ x+2 & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ x-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-2 \\\\ x(1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)) & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-2 \\\\ x & =\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-2}{1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534579 true] [17592186296728 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296729 13194139534579 true] [17592186296728 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534579 true] [17592186296728 1041 "field-1" 13194139534579 true] [17592186296728 1104 #edb/ref 17592186296729 13194139534579 true] [17592186296728 1110 #uuid "531ee5d0-a628-5849-860b-4cc02b16d934" 13194139534579 true] [17592186296729 1034 "\\frac{3\\ln(2)-2}{1-\\ln(2)}" 13194139534579 true] [17592186296729 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534579 true] [17592186296729 1111 #uuid "a4635ab6-c06d-59a5-a5d1-b19ecc37ab1e" 13194139534579 true] [17592186296730 1017 #edb/ref 17592186296731 13194139534579 true] [17592186296730 1089 "q-242904" 13194139534579 true] [17592186296730 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534579 true] [17592186296730 1100 "Expressed in terms of natural logarithms, determine the value of $x$ that satisfies the equation ${e}^{2x-2}=2\\cdot {9}^{x}.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534579 true] [17592186296730 1113 #uuid "eb2badcc-b8ec-5da1-a517-670e53be7625" 13194139534579 true] [17592186296730 1145 "First, we take the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2x-2} & =2\\cdot {9}^{x} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2x-2}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\cdot {9}^{x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{a})=a$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n2x-2=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\cdot {9}^{x}).\n$$\n\nNext, we use the power and product laws of logarithms to simplify the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-2 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({9}^{x}) \\\\ 2x-2 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-2 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9) \\\\ 2x-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9) & =2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ x(2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9)) & =2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ x & =\\frac{2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}{2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534579 true] [17592186296731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296732 13194139534579 true] [17592186296731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296733 13194139534579 true] [17592186296731 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534579 true] [17592186296731 1041 "field-1" 13194139534579 true] [17592186296731 1104 #edb/ref 17592186296732 13194139534579 true] [17592186296731 1110 #uuid "8bfff3ad-889e-5faa-88dd-7cf4136957f8" 13194139534579 true] [17592186296732 1034 "\\frac{2+\\ln(2)}{2-\\ln(9)}" 13194139534579 true] [17592186296732 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534579 true] [17592186296732